  <h1>Harmonic Resonance &amp; Coupled Processes</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    Low-integer ratios are not aesthetic ornament. Whenever two recurrent processes couple across a port —
    guarded streams in an interaction net, clockless GALS silicon tiles, distributed peers, or neural oscillators —
    their relative rate $\rho = \omega_A / \omega_B$ governs bounded memory, phase-locking stability,
    beating drift, and anti-resonant independence.
  </p>

