  <h2 id="balance">1. Bounded $O(1)$ Memory Is a Rational Resonance Condition</h2>
  <p>
    In Hyperactivity, an ongoing computation is a guarded corecursive process ($\triangleright\,\kappa$) whose
    local state advances in discrete interaction steps. Consider two coupled processes $A$ and $B$ connected by a
    finite channel: each firing of $A$ emits $p \in \mathbb{N}^+$ tokens, and each firing of $B$ consumes
    $q \in \mathbb{N}^+$ tokens. Over a window of $k_A$ firings of $A$ and $k_B$ firings of $B$, the net change in
    buffer occupancy is $\Delta = k_A p - k_B q$.
  </p>
  <p>
    For a global cyclic computation to run forever in <strong>strictly bounded $O(1)$ local memory</strong>
    (the <code>memory-is-local</code> invariant of Hyperactivity and clockless GALS silicon tiles in
    <a href="/silicon">/silicon</a>), the topology must admit a non-zero integer firing vector satisfying the
    <strong>Karp–Miller / Lee–Messerschmitt balance equation</strong>:
  </p>
  $$k_A \cdot p \;=\; k_B \cdot q \quad\Longleftrightarrow\quad \frac{\omega_A}{\omega_B} \;=\; \frac{q}{p} \in \mathbb{Q}^+.$$
  <p>
    If the rates sit on the exact rational ratio $q/p$, the buffer returns to its exact initial occupancy every
    $(q, p)$ firings. If $\omega_A$ is detuned off resonance, the residual flow accumulates linearly into
    unbounded queue growth — or, under credit-based GALS backpressure handshaking, forces periodic stall waves
    whose frequency is the exact <strong>beat frequency</strong> $|\omega_A p - \omega_B q|$.
  </p>

  <div class="thm">
