  <h2 id="tongues">2. Why Simple Ratios Win: The Stern–Brocot Tree &amp; Arnold Tongues</h2>
  <p>
    Not all rational ratios are equally robust. When two nonlinear recurrent oscillators couple with strength $K$
    — whether phase-locked loops on silicon, coupled FitzHugh–Nagumo neurons in <a href="/neuro">/neuro</a>, or
    distributed peers exchanging periodic heartbeats — their discrete phase dynamics follow the
    <strong>standard circle map</strong>:
  </p>
  $$\theta_{n+1} \;=\; \theta_n + \Omega - \frac{K}{2\pi}\sin(2\pi\theta_n) \pmod{1}.$$
  <p>
    Even when the bare frequency ratio $\Omega$ drifts slightly away from a rational $p/q$, coupling $K > 0$ pulls
    the effective winding number $W = \lim_{n\to\infty}(\theta_n - \theta_0)/n$ into an exact rational lock $p/q$.
    The locking region in $(\Omega, K)$-space is an <strong>Arnold tongue</strong>, and its width shrinks rapidly
    with the denominator $q$. The natural hierarchy of synchronization stability is the
    <strong>Stern–Brocot tree</strong>, where every new rational is born as the <em>mediant</em> of its two
    unimodular Farey parents:
  </p>
  $$\frac{p_1}{q_1} \;\oplus\; \frac{p_2}{q_2} \;=\; \frac{p_1 + p_2}{q_1 + q_2}, \qquad p_2 q_1 - p_1 q_2 = 1.$$
  <p>
    Because the Farey interval width between unimodular neighbors is $\frac{1}{q_1 q_2}$, shallow tree nodes
    ($1/1$, $1/2$, $2/3$, $3/4$, $2/5$) own the widest, most noise-tolerant basins of attraction. Conversely, the
    alternating spine <code>R, L, R, L, …</code> generates the Fibonacci ratios $F_{n+1}/F_n \to \varphi$
    (the golden ratio $[1;1,1,1,\dots]$), which stays <strong>maximally far from every low-order tongue</strong>.
    In systems design, this creates three distinct behavioral regimes:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Low-height rational lock ($1:1, 2:1, 3:2, 4:3$):</strong> coherent binding, noise-tolerant handoff, minimum synchronization overhead.</li>
    <li><strong>Near-resonance detuning:</strong> slow beat envelope / phase precession sweeping through all relative phases (used in hippocampal theta-gamma coding).</li>
    <li><strong>Noble irrational ($\varphi$):</strong> anti-resonant isolation — concurrent subsystems avoid locking onto each other (preventing destructive interference or pathological synchrony).</li>
  </ul>

